{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s8CopyableP"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A finite directed graph on the vertices "},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose out-neighbors come from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure, called on demand and never stored: an implicit graph (Boost’s "},{"code":"grid_graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"GridGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"FullGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). It is a lawful "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so every generic algorithm runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on it, including those that need the whole vertex set (components, centrality), with no edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For a state space with no vertex collection (an unbounded grid, a puzzle), use the closure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"searches instead: Traversal’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"breadthFirstSearch(from:successors:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ShortestPaths’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"dijkstraShortestPath(from:successors:success:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"aStarShortestPath(from:successors: heuristic:success:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" states over a finite set, number them and use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LabeledGraph<State, ImplicitDirectedGraph<Row>>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a grid is numbered row-major.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The closure.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(v)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the targets of the edges leaving "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":", once per edge, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence<Int>"},{"type":"text","text":" (an array, a lazy filter over a fixed neighbor list), so a specialized build"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inlines it with no type erasure. Each read of a row calls it once: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outDegree(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" once each, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":" once"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per vertex. It must return the same sequence each time it is asked about the same vertex (the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol’s “asking again gives the same answer”); this is documented, not checked, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure that breaks it breaks every algorithm, as a mutating "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":" breaks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Set"},{"type":"text","text":". Each target is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"checked to be a vertex when it is read, not when the row is formed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Positions.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" An edge’s position is ","type":"text"},{"code":"Edges.Index","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": its source, its rank in the source’s row,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and its target. Equality, order and hashing use ","type":"text"},{"code":"(source, rank)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", unique even among parallel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edges and self-loops; the target rides along, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"source(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"target(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"weight closure reading ","type":"text"},{"code":"$0.target","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call nothing. There are no dense edge indices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":": a closure has no identity and is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift#L32"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"}],"externalID":"s:14ImplicitGraphs0A13DirectedGraphV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"ImplicitGraphs"}],"title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","symbolKind":"struct"},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","generated":true,"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/OutEdges","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors"]},{"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/init(vertexCount:successors:)"]},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/DirectedGraph-Implementations"]}],"references":{"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs/ImplicitDirectedGraph/Successors":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors","typ